Z||000000||firstfiero||05-04-2001||10:43 AM||||       One of my dash speakers blew! driving me crazy...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"> . Anyway...what size are the origingal speakers. Does anybody have any sitting around out their? I don't want anything expensive I'm not into loud stereo's but I dont like to hear  BONG...BUNG...BUNG all the time either!<P>------------------<BR>Hey Mr. Ricer come over here and tell me how your stickers make you faster.....<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/headshot.gif">     <BR>Todd <BR>  86se<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/photo3.jpg"> ||||reg||13
Z||000001||Black88GT||05-04-2001||10:51 AM||||They are 4x10.  You can get good aftermarket replacements from Pioneer or Kenwood for less then 100 bucks for the pair.  Well worth it over the stock speakers.<P>Also as a side note, try to make that pic in your sig a little smaller, I know some people have 56k and it takes a while to load, also scrolling down the screen with a couple of those sigs can get tiresome.  Nice car though! ||||reg||7
Z||000002||JSocha||05-04-2001||10:53 AM||||Front speakers are 4x10's (which have also been phased out by many speaker manufacturers because of their odd size.  Kenwood & Pioneer are the last still to manufacture but also from what I have heard from local stereo shops, they are phasing out there 4x10 speaker lines as well.  Getting to be like pulling hens teeth!).<P>Rear speakers if I recall are 4x6, at least I believe they are on my 87GT.<P>Are you looking for a STOCK speaker (made out of paper)?  Or are you thinking on upgrading to a "better" set of quality speakers that will be able to handle the bad Thud problem and add more to your listening enjoyment?<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jnjsochasig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Oreif||05-04-2001||02:22 PM||||There are only 3 manufacturer's of 4X10 dash speakers. Pioneer, Kenwood, and Pyle. All other's have stopped making them. All the above are less than $100 per pair. In the sail panels are 4X6 speakers. Many folks still make them in a 4X6 speaker or a 3.5" woofer with seperate tweeter on a 4X6 plate.<BR>The sound of the Pioneers are generally the better sounding. If you plan to replace the fronts, I would recommend replacing them all.<BR>It's not hard to do and the improvements will be great. Also the higher quality of the speakers means they will last a long time.||||reg||1
Z||000004||stimpy||05-04-2001||02:23 PM||||If you are really budget minded, Audiovox makes 4x10 replacement speakers for like $25 a pair. They are CRAP, but better then a blown out 16 year old paper cone speaker. (not much tho) They can be found at places like Pep Boys, Grand Auto, etc. Maybe even Wa Mart!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>I recommend ponying up the Franklin for the Pioneers. They are great and will outlast the rest of your car hooked up to the stock system.||||reg||1
