Z||000011||Mach10||05-05-2001||12:48 PM||||I can't stand 4x10s   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><BR>You'd be better off getting a set of 4" w/components and building a plate to mount them on. Personally, the first thing I'm going to do when my car's ready will be to cut the dash to make room for a set of 5-1/4s. If I have too, maybe a set of 5x7s, but I've just never liked the sound from oval speakers. Not quantative, but I've always prefered spending more on smaller speakers. I don't need base from a component. That's what the subs and mids are for   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Mach10 (edited 05-05-2001).]||||reg||7
Z||000012||Seanh||05-05-2001||04:36 PM||||Yeah, I agree, get 4" Components. Atleast 4" Coax's if you have to. Round speakers will sound better the oval's. Put some bass blockers (cap's) on there also to keep the low bass out of them. Probally cross them over at like 100Hz.||||reg||1
